  <static seed="195" source="Library/Michigan/Chap5Sec3/Q11.pg">
    <statement><p>Find the average value of 
<m>f(x)=6 x + 3</m> over <m>[1,3]</m></p>
<p>average value = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>15</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f</m> on
<m>1\le x\le 3</m>.  The integral is the area under the curve, which is a 
trapezoidal area.  So the average value is
<me>\mbox{average} = \frac1{3-1} \int_{1}^{3} (6 x+3)\,dx = 
  \frac1{2}\cdot\frac{9+21}{2}\cdot 2 = 15.</me>



</solution>
